  "caveat": "This table establishes a REAL evolutionary-conservation gradient across C. elegans ion-channel and synaptic genes: orthologue percent-identity to related Caenorhabditis species (briggsae/remanei/brenneri/japonica, Ensembl Metazoa REST homology) spans a wide range, identifying highly conserved ('stiff') vs more divergent ('sloppy') channel genes. HOWEVER, a direct correlation between this conservation gradient and our simulator's per-channel stiff/sloppy (Hessian) ranking is NOT yet possible: our worm sims (BAAIWorm / modWorm) calibrate global mechanism-CLASS scalings (synaptic / gap-junction / ionic / passive), not per-channel parameters. Mapping per-gene conservation onto per-channel sensitivity requires the per-channel Hessian, which is compute-deferred. Numbers are pulled live from Ensembl REST and are not fabricated; genes with no mappable symbol or no Caenorhabditis ortholog are listed under 'not_found'."
}